{%- comment -%}
  The design tokens of the blog post. Shared, because the post's COMPONENTS are shared:
  sections/dev-article.liquid renders the real post, and sections/dev-article-components.liquid
  renders the component library page (live examples through the same snippets/dev-article-body.liquid
  and the same assets/dev-article.css). If the library page kept its own copy of these values, the
  examples an editor copies from would drift from the post they paste into — the first time anyone
  touched either file.

  Every value's provenance is recorded in the header comment of sections/dev-article.liquid.
  Same pattern as snippets/dev-journal-card-tokens.liquid.

  @param {string} scope - CSS selector of the calling section's root, e.g. '.dev-article'
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  {{ scope }} {

    --section-px: 64px;
    --section-px-m: 16px;

    {%- comment -%} Three widths. --measure is the reading column. --media-w is the wider container
       the hero image fills, so the photo has presence without the prose inheriting a 960px line.
       --container-max is the page container every measured section shares (1440 − 2×64); only the
       >= 1280 TOC rail ever reaches it. See the header comment. {%- endcomment -%}
    --measure: 720px;
    --media-w: 960px;
    --container-max: 1312px;
    --rail-w: 256px;

    --font-title-size: 48px;
    --font-title-size-m: 32px;
    --font-title-weight: 500;
    --font-title-lh: 1.2;

    --font-deck-size: 20px;
    --font-deck-size-m: 18px;

    {%- comment -%} Body copy and the headings INSIDE the article body. The body h2/h3 step down from the
       title rather than repeating it, so the page has one obvious top. {%- endcomment -%}
    --font-body-size: 18px;
    --font-body-size-m: 16px;
    --font-body-weight: 500;
    --font-body-lh: 1.6; {%- comment -%} looser than the 1.4 the cards use: those are 2-line captions, this is prose {%- endcomment -%}
    --font-h2-size: 32px;
    --font-h3-size: 22px;

    --font-meta-size: 16px;
    --font-badge-size: 14px;
    --font-bold: 700;

    {%- comment -%} Panels: TOC, top tip, icon breakdown. dev-pdp-guarantees' panel-and-tile pair. {%- endcomment -%}
    --font-panel-title-size: 22px;
    --font-panel-title-size-m: 20px;
    --font-panel-size: 16px;
    --font-panel-lh: 1.4;
    --panel-pad: 24px;
    --panel-pad-m: 16px;
    --icon-tile: 48px;

    {%- comment -%} The quote box. UPRIGHT, not italic, on purpose: Tiempos Medium Italic is still the
       67-glyph TRIAL cut (snippets/dev-brand-fonts.liquid) with no ’ “ ” – £ é — and a pull quote
       is exactly where curly punctuation lives. In italic, "Caring for a duvet isn’t hard" swaps
       font mid-word at the apostrophe. When the licensed Medium Italic lands, change this ONE token
       to `italic` and nothing else moves (the retail cuts are metric-compatible). {%- endcomment -%}
    --font-quote-size: 28px;
    --font-quote-size-m: 22px;
    --font-quote-style: normal;
    --quote-mark: 40px;

    --spacing-xs: 8px;
    --spacing-sm: 16px;
    --spacing-md: 24px;
    --spacing-lg: 32px;
    --spacing-xl: 48px;
    --spacing-2xl: 64px;

    {%- comment -%} Hero crop. 3:2 is the shape a camera hands you, so it is the least violent thing to impose
       on photography a merchant did not shoot for this slot — and unlike `height: auto` it is the
       SAME shape for every article, portrait uploads included. At the 960px container that is
       960x640, comfortably inside one screen, with the first paragraph visible under it.

       One value for both breakpoints, which is this theme's habit (story-slider and
       values-we-cherish do the same): the ratio is the design, not a per-device measurement. {%- endcomment -%}
    --ratio-media: 3 / 2;

    --radius-media: 32px;
    --radius-inline: 16px;
    --radius-badge: 60px;

    --icon-size: 24px;
    --avatar: 48px;

    {%- comment -%} dev-faq's accordion timing, verbatim. dev-article.js reads --acc-dur back out (in ms). {%- endcomment -%}
    --acc-dur: 300ms;
    --acc-ease: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1);

    {%- comment -%} Where the sticky rail parks, and where an anchor jump lands. The site header is sticky and
       slides back in on scroll-up, so a heading jumped to must clear it: 96px is the header bar
       (~72) plus the --spacing-md breathing room. {%- endcomment -%}
    --rail-top: 48px;
    --anchor-offset: 96px;
  }
</style>
